WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.250
February 25th (Thursday)

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:11.880
Hey!

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:19.140
What? Have you gotten lost?

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:20.560
I finally found you.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:24.060
February 29th (Monday)

00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:29.820
"He decided not to go out
for it began to rain."

00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:32.450
The "for" in this sentence is a conjunction...

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:32.450
Chi...

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:09.710
Devils have possessed this park!

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:15.220
The lands of Musashino are corrupted by
the electromagnetic waves of Wardenclyffe!

00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:17.430
This park is, too, of course!

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:20.430
The experiments of Nikola Tesla
are still continuing!

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:25.310
That is indeed the global system
created by the Tokyo Radio Tower!

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:25.310
<i>You've already noticed me
gazing at you.</i>

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:27.190
Such a cute guy.

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:31.900
Two large antennae point
toward the Musashino area 24 hours a day!

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.270
Huh? That's weird.

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:34.530
I was told by the Yafoo! Auction seller
that they'd deliver the Vanguard card here.

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:35.780
They are doing so confidently
as people look around!

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:38.530
Maybe I shouldn't have trusted
personal delivery after all.

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:39.110
People not openly showing their anger
is proof that they are brainwashed!

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:40.990
Oh, maybe you're the one
I made the deal with?

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:44.490
Oh, my handle is "Domo, I'm Zenigata."

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:47.120
I'm sorry, but I don't know
what you're talking about.

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:48.500
Oh, pardon me.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:52.630
Actually, I made a successful bid
on a rare Vangua card on an internet auction.

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:55.630
The seller specified here
as the rendezvous point.

00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:57.130
I chose personal delivery

00:02:57.130 --> 00:02:59.930
so that I could brag about it
as soon as possible to all the snotty brats.

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:01.970
But it seems like I was careless
and I was duped.

00:03:02.470 --> 00:03:04.220
Man, I made a mistake!

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:08.100
But lately I hear there are many
beautiful female Vangua players like you,

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:13.400
and so I approached you
with a faint expectation of sorts. Yeah.

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:17.570
You're a cute student.
Are you cosplaying?

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:19.990
Despite my look,
I'm a college graduate with a job.

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:22.200
This is my work attire, too.

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:25.580
That means you must be older than me.

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:28.620
But still, my personal impression
is that you are...

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:30.120
rather cute.

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:35.130
You just took
something very important to me.

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:39.130
Oh, can you tell me
what this important thing is?

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:41.430
My heart.

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:46.390
The corruption is not just in Musashino!

00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:50.140
It's not just Tokyo, it's not just Japan!

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:49.310
By the way, what in the world
is that old man?

00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:50.390
He is "god."

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:54.110
It's already starting
to spread all over the world!

00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:52.600
You are acquaintances with a god?

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:54.110
No, I don't know him.

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:55.770
But you're drawing that old ma—

00:03:55.770 --> 00:03:57.150
"god."

00:03:57.150 --> 00:03:58.780
I'm doing it on my own accord.

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:00.070
He doesn't get mad at you?

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:02.240
Contrary to expectations, it seems okay.

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:04.870
I'm sure "god" is very tolerant.

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:06.990
Can I take a look?

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:10.500
Oh, this is really well done!

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:12.830
Are you a part of a wall-side circle?

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:16.130
No, wait. But this isn't
what you'd call moe art per se.

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:17.340
But it's really well done!

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:19.920
It looks like I've seen
this art style somewhere, too.

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:21.930
Are you a student?
Do you go to art school?

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:26.050
No, I'm a student, but not of art school.
I go to Seimei University right over there.

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:28.470
Do they have
an art department over there?

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:29.470
They don't.

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:31.690
Your art is too good
for an ordinary student!

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:33.560
That's right, this is Kichijoji!

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:35.770
Many manga artists live in Kichijoji.

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:37.650
That means
you're a manga artist, as well?

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:39.150
Please, can I shake your hand?

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:41.570
If you do, I'll never wash my hands again
for the rest of my life!

00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:43.240
A manga artist yes,
but I'm a doujin artist.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:46.620
That means, you participate
in Comiket, as well? What's your genre?

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:49.620
Boys' Love would be out of my radar...

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:53.580
But anyway, I think I've seen
this art style somewhere in the past.

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:55.420
You're lying to me, aren't you?

00:04:55.420 --> 00:05:00.210
Where did you see one of my books?
I'd like to hear. Let me hear.

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:02.720
If all of this isn't a lie
that you used as a pick-up line.

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:06.720
But I seriously can't remember.
I'm so lame!

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:08.600
Right now, I'm really lame!

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:11.270
I'm sorry, but can you
tell me your name?

00:05:11.270 --> 00:05:14.230
It's okay if you tell me the title
of a doujin book you've authored instead.

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:15.850
I may have read that book.

00:05:16.190 --> 00:05:17.650
My name is Ririka Nishizono—

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:18.730
Yes, I know that.

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:22.240
So you did know from the beginning.

00:05:22.650 --> 00:05:24.030
You're such a sneaky person.

00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:27.990
Your "A Dark Water's Bottom"
is the talk of the internet lately.

00:05:27.990 --> 00:05:29.030
Did you know that?

00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:31.700
- Are you really talking about the internet?
- Of course.

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:34.410
By "talk" you mean something like
"that book wasn't interesting" and such?

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:38.130
Right. I did read it myself,
and indeed, it wasn't interesting at all.

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:41.170
But the topic was quite interesting.

00:05:41.170 --> 00:05:43.800
Especially the story of the third chapter.
That was marvelous!

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:46.890
The third chapter?
Wasn't Boys' Love off your radar?

00:05:46.890 --> 00:05:50.810
It is. But the content itself
was something very interesting.

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:56.390
I'd been wanting all this time to ask you
how you came up with that story.

00:05:56.390 --> 00:06:00.360
I mean, people normally don't think
of gouging out a tooth with a knife

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:03.990
as a memento
after killing someone you love.

00:06:05.110 --> 00:06:07.700
I don't think up any ideas.

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:12.160
Everything I draw are all based
on the dreams I've had.

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:19.580
Anyway, about the CODE...

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:21.590
A cord? Like for earphones?

00:06:21.590 --> 00:06:22.960
No, that's not it!

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:25.880
The one spelled out C-O-D-E. CODE.

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:27.010
I don't know much of it.

00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:29.050
If you're drawing manga
based on the dreams you saw,

00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:30.970
are those dreams foresights?

00:06:32.260 --> 00:06:36.940
This is a copy of a page from
"A Dark Water's Bottom" that you drew.

00:06:37.310 --> 00:06:40.360
There are letters written in the spot
where I circled with red.

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:42.980
Letters of the alphabet.
What did you write here?

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:46.070
- COLA.
- That's not it!

00:06:46.070 --> 00:06:48.450
You understand, right?
You were the one that drew this.

00:06:49.610 --> 00:06:50.450
You're right.

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:51.950
This is CODE.

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:54.330
So, what's the big deal about that?

00:06:56.540 --> 00:06:58.960
A photograph that has
something to do with my work?

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:02.960
This is a dying message that the victim
of a certain murder had left behind.

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:04.840
Who are you?

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:08.970
You don't have to ask.
You should already know me pretty well.

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:10.550
After all, despite my look...

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:13.810
I'm the detective in your manga.

00:07:15.350 --> 00:07:16.470
Truly delicious!

00:07:16.850 --> 00:07:18.600
Truly tasty!

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:22.730
Isn't it, isn't it? Why can't Gamota
realize the wonderfulness of this flavor?

00:07:23.270 --> 00:07:25.690
He's not here again today.

00:07:25.940 --> 00:07:28.190
Maybe he caught an off-season cold.

00:07:28.190 --> 00:07:30.030
It seems like he is home, though.

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:31.280
Oh, is that so?

00:07:31.530 --> 00:07:34.830
The last I heard Gamotan's voice
was when he answered the phone

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:37.200
in a really depressing voice.

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:40.540
Stop dramatizing it in an ominous way.

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:45.090
Oh, I'm sorry, I have to step out a bit.

00:07:45.090 --> 00:07:46.000
Oh?

00:07:45.710 --> 00:07:47.170
Hello?

00:07:46.710 --> 00:07:48.300
Take care!

00:07:50.130 --> 00:07:50.800
Oh, my...

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:54.470
Receipt
66,600 yen - Consulting fees
Kurenaino Aria

00:07:51.260 --> 00:07:54.010
That's why I said
let's do a special on devils.

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:56.010
Here's Gamotan!

00:07:58.730 --> 00:08:00.560
No. Oh, yes.

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:02.520
I'll return right away. See you.

00:08:03.610 --> 00:08:07.610
Izumin, I'm gonna go home
for today! Bye!

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:09.070
Okay, see ya!

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:19.200
Sarai Hashigami?

00:08:20.910 --> 00:08:21.870
Hello there.

00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:25.420
You were the one closest to him,
but you ended up being the last one.

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:29.380
I heard that you didn't speak
with your father too much.

00:08:29.380 --> 00:08:32.180
Right. We didn't have
a good relationship.

00:08:32.510 --> 00:08:35.890
Especially after committing himself
to bogus ideas like the occult.

00:08:35.890 --> 00:08:38.180
Which means you respected him
a bit until then?

00:08:39.310 --> 00:08:40.140
<i>Nonsense!</i>

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:43.140
<i>Dad, are you going to sacrifice
everything you've worked for?</i>

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:47.110
<i>There is nothing that cannot be a subject
of science. That includes the occult.</i>

00:08:47.110 --> 00:08:51.150
<i>You know how many people were
driven out from academia by saying that?</i>

00:08:51.150 --> 00:08:54.780
<i>I also know that their intent
was not corrupt.</i>

00:08:55.370 --> 00:08:58.990
<i>Dad, their hearts
may not have been corrupt.</i>

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:01.960
<i>But people that can see things
that can't be seen,</i>

00:09:01.960 --> 00:09:06.420
<i>the hearts of people that can do things
others can't do... They're often corrupt!</i>

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:09.420
<i>Let's say that there really is a world
where human knowledge falls short.</i>

00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:11.420
<i>But there's no way for you to prove</i>

00:09:11.420 --> 00:09:13.800
<i>that the people who act as mediators
for that world are just!</i>

00:09:14.180 --> 00:09:18.300
<i>If they're lying,
then they're the only ones who'll know!</i>

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:20.720
<i>There is no mistake in what you say.</i>

00:09:20.970 --> 00:09:22.810
<i>But there must be some way.</i>

00:09:23.390 --> 00:09:25.060
<i>And I want to find it.</i>

00:09:25.060 --> 00:09:28.480
<i>Dad, you said so often that you were
going to make the super-theory</i>

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:30.190
<i>left behind by Nikola Tesla into reality!</i>

00:09:30.190 --> 00:09:31.150
<i>Yet, why...</i>

00:09:31.150 --> 00:09:34.780
<i>I figured it out as I explored deeper
into the research Tesla left behind.</i>

00:09:35.030 --> 00:09:41.490
<i>He may have found a world where the spiritual
bodies, conscious astral forms, gathered.</i>

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:43.960
<i>I want to prove that.</i>

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:46.920
<i>Spiritual bodies? Dad, are you sane?</i>

00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:49.040
<i>Fine, you can do whatever you want!</i>

00:09:56.340 --> 00:09:57.640
Science and engineering...

00:09:58.010 --> 00:10:02.470
Professor Hashigami, an authority
trying to resolve Tesla's super-theory

00:10:02.470 --> 00:10:05.270
that had long been a mystery,
suddenly turned to the occult.

00:10:05.980 --> 00:10:08.440
I think there was some catalyst
for him to do so.

00:10:08.690 --> 00:10:10.150
I don't know anything of the sort.

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:11.900
It was all too sudden.

00:10:12.280 --> 00:10:16.610
Because you're his son by blood,
you're furthest from the truth.

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:19.660
This kid's the same as that other kid.

00:10:20.410 --> 00:10:23.540
By the way, have you heard
something about the Aveline Note?

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:25.660
What's that?

00:10:25.910 --> 00:10:27.420
If you don't know, that's fine.
Forget it.

00:10:27.920 --> 00:10:29.040
Also, for today and tomorrow,

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:31.170
it's better for you
if you kept your cell phone turned off.

00:10:31.170 --> 00:10:32.130
What do you mean?

00:10:32.630 --> 00:10:34.670
I'd like to talk to you again sometime.

00:10:42.180 --> 00:10:45.560
<i>My parents passed away
when I was only ten years old.</i>

00:10:46.730 --> 00:10:51.610
<i>Ever since, in this needlessly spacious
mansion, I lived alone with Big Brother.</i>

00:10:49.520 --> 00:10:50.440
<i>Ria...</i>

00:10:51.610 --> 00:10:52.650
<i>Big Brother!</i>

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:56.900
<i>Big Brother was someone I aspired to be.</i>

00:10:57.150 --> 00:11:00.070
<i>I was happy merely by spending time
together with Big Brother.</i>

00:11:00.780 --> 00:11:02.910
<i>Nowadays, I don't know
how much Big Brother sacrificed</i>

00:11:02.530 --> 00:11:03.620
<i>I'm home.</i>

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:08.330
<i>to raise my young self,
13 years younger than him.</i>

00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:05.620
<i>Welcome home!</i>

00:11:10.630 --> 00:11:13.040
<i>School was full of hardship.</i>

00:11:17.090 --> 00:11:21.260
<i>I don't want to go anywhere else.
I don't want you to go anywhere else.</i>

00:11:21.260 --> 00:11:24.220
<i>Please, Big Brother.
Please don't go to work.</i>

00:11:24.220 --> 00:11:27.020
<i>If you go, I'll bite my tongue
and kill myself!</i>

00:11:27.310 --> 00:11:29.480
<i>I feel the same way as you do, Ria.</i>

00:11:29.480 --> 00:11:32.230
<i>I want to spend forever
quietly living together with you.</i>

00:11:32.230 --> 00:11:37.030
<i>But for us to keep living,
I have no choice but to go do some work.</i>

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:38.400
<i>I'm sorry, Ria.</i>

00:11:39.570 --> 00:11:42.910
<i>When I turned 14,
there was a drastic change.</i>

00:11:45.910 --> 00:11:48.410
<i>Ria! Ria! Ria!</i>

00:11:46.410 --> 00:11:49.040
<i>I collapsed from hyperventilation.</i>

00:11:49.290 --> 00:11:53.420
<i>Ever since then, Big Brother quit his job
and stayed at home all day.</i>

00:11:53.790 --> 00:11:58.670
<i>That one year, I believe,
was the most fulfilling time of my life.</i>

00:11:59.090 --> 00:12:01.300
<i>My dreams from childhood
finally came true.</i>

00:12:01.840 --> 00:12:04.640
<i>I was able to persevere
all my classmates, my male teachers</i>

00:12:04.640 --> 00:12:07.390
<i>and suspicious men leering at me.</i>

00:12:08.270 --> 00:12:10.850
<i>Ria, you're a very charming girl,</i>

00:12:10.850 --> 00:12:14.060
<i>so perhaps the men all go crazy
from that charm.</i>

00:12:14.360 --> 00:12:19.280
<i>I want to protect you, Ria,
but I can't go to school with you.</i>

00:12:19.490 --> 00:12:21.400
<i>I'll be fine, Big Brother.</i>

00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:23.910
<i>As long as I can have you
holding me like this,</i>

00:12:23.910 --> 00:12:26.410
<i>I can persevere through anything,
no matter how unpleasant.</i>

00:12:26.410 --> 00:12:28.040
<i>That's admirable, Ria.</i>

00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:32.040
<i>But if someone gives you a hard time,
you must tell me, okay?</i>

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:35.840
<i>I'll take any means possible
to retaliate.</i>

00:12:36.090 --> 00:12:38.250
<i>I won't let them
approach you ever again, Ria.</i>

00:12:38.840 --> 00:12:40.920
<i>Thank you, Big Brother.</i>

00:12:41.300 --> 00:12:42.300
<i>I love you.</i>

00:12:42.760 --> 00:12:46.050
<i>However, that happiness was short-lived.</i>

00:13:00.030 --> 00:13:01.700
<i>Who are all of you?</i>

00:13:01.700 --> 00:13:04.780
<i>What are you doing to Big Brother?
Don't touch Big Brother!</i>

00:13:04.780 --> 00:13:07.530
<i>You're trying to take my big brother
away on your own discretion!</i>

00:13:07.530 --> 00:13:10.370
<i>This is an abduction!
You all leave here right away!</i>

00:13:10.370 --> 00:13:13.120
<i>- Ria, calm down.
- How can I can stay calm?</i>

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:16.420
<i>My only family member is about to be
taken away right in front of me!</i>

00:13:16.420 --> 00:13:18.750
<i>Big Brother!
Please wake up, Big Brother!</i>

00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:20.010
<i>Big Brother!</i>

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:23.880
<i>Big Brother!</i>

00:13:24.680 --> 00:13:26.590
<i>Someone! Hold Ria down!</i>

00:13:26.850 --> 00:13:30.020
<i>Don't take him away!
Don't take Big Brother away from me!</i>

00:13:30.180 --> 00:13:33.020
<i>No! Let go! Big Brother!</i>

00:13:31.100 --> 00:13:34.980
<i>Stop thrashing! How long are you going to
continue such a horrific thing!</i>

00:13:33.020 --> 00:13:34.980
<i>Help me, Big Brother!</i>

00:13:34.980 --> 00:13:36.350
<i>This isn't... normal!</i>

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:37.810
<i>This is abnormal!</i>

00:13:39.770 --> 00:13:40.610
<i>Abnormal?</i>

00:13:50.240 --> 00:13:52.080
<i>Abnormal, you say?</i>

00:13:57.000 --> 00:13:59.000
<i>You must be thinking
I'm alluring Big Brother</i>

00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:01.840
<i>and we're committing incest, right?</i>

00:14:01.840 --> 00:14:05.300
<i>To show such prejudice just because
a girl has a fancy for black magic!</i>

00:14:05.300 --> 00:14:08.680
<i>All you adults are quite a bit more
horrendous than I am!</i>

00:14:09.050 --> 00:14:12.060
<i>It's true that I love my big brother.</i>

00:14:12.350 --> 00:14:16.310
<i>However, not once have we gotten
into such a sinful relationship!</i>

00:14:16.310 --> 00:14:20.190
<i>What's wrong with two siblings
being together and loving each other purely?</i>

00:14:20.190 --> 00:14:22.730
<i>This story is beyond that level, Ria!</i>

00:14:22.730 --> 00:14:25.450
<i>Reality... Can't you see
this scene in reality?</i>

00:14:26.280 --> 00:14:27.950
<i>Reality?</i>

00:14:27.950 --> 00:14:30.450
<i>There was a police report
from the neighbors</i>

00:14:30.450 --> 00:14:32.870
<i>that there was a horrendous
rotting smell coming from this house!</i>

00:14:32.870 --> 00:14:35.330
<i>What do you mean by that?
What in the world are you talking—</i>

00:14:35.790 --> 00:14:37.370
<i>Listen up, Ria.</i>

00:14:37.370 --> 00:14:38.540
<i>Your big brother...</i>

00:14:38.880 --> 00:14:40.840
<i>passed away a good year ago!</i>

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:46.420
<i>That can't be true.
I mean, Big Brother is right there—</i>

00:14:55.730 --> 00:14:56.890
A medical error?

00:14:56.890 --> 00:14:57.560
Yes.

00:14:56.890 --> 00:14:57.890
MONTHLY MUMU

00:14:56.890 --> 00:14:57.890
EDITORIAL DIVISION 3

00:14:57.890 --> 00:15:00.190
Three years ago,
at Tokyo Medical University in Hachioji,

00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:04.070
there was a kidney transplant operation
from the older brother, Takaharu Minase,

00:15:04.070 --> 00:15:06.570
to his younger sister Ria.
Takaharu passed away during the operation.

00:15:06.820 --> 00:15:09.110
Ria's progress post-surgery
was quite well.

00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:13.830
Ria, upon waking, couldn't accept
the death of her dearest big brother.

00:15:10.320 --> 00:15:12.830
Living Donor Kidney Transplant
Failed in Tokyo

00:15:14.080 --> 00:15:18.000
A few days later, Takaharu Minase's corpse
disappeared from the morgue.

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:19.790
A mere 14 year old girl, to redeem herself,

00:15:19.790 --> 00:15:23.040
put the corpse of her
dead big brother on a wheelchair

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:25.010
and walked all the way back home.

00:15:25.010 --> 00:15:26.260
From Hachioji?

00:15:26.510 --> 00:15:29.680
Yes. She walked home
from Hachioji to Kichijoji.

00:15:29.680 --> 00:15:31.510
That's roughly 20 kilometers
as the crow flies.

00:15:31.510 --> 00:15:35.640
A girl who just received a kidney transplant,
pushing a wheelchair carrying a corpse...

00:15:36.140 --> 00:15:40.440
And once home, Ria started living
together with her big brother's corpse.

00:15:40.690 --> 00:15:43.980
In the end, her relatives found out,
and all of that ended after a year.

00:15:44.230 --> 00:15:45.530
Now, listen up, Editor-in-chief.

00:15:45.860 --> 00:15:47.360
This is where it gets interesting!

00:15:47.610 --> 00:15:51.320
Even now, Ria Minase lives all alone
in the very same house.

00:15:51.320 --> 00:15:53.830
Furthermore, she changed
her name to Kurenaino Aria

00:15:53.830 --> 00:15:56.540
and now operates as an agent
to perform black magic for others.

00:15:56.540 --> 00:15:59.250
I'm sure she's definitely
up to doing something.

00:16:00.920 --> 00:16:03.960
<i>Was all of it my fantasy?</i>

00:16:04.380 --> 00:16:06.800
<i>All those wonderful days...</i>

00:16:07.840 --> 00:16:11.300
<i>I don't know.
I can't come to conclusions myself.</i>

00:16:14.800 --> 00:16:17.270
Private Number

00:16:17.680 --> 00:16:18.810
Private Number

00:16:23.650 --> 00:16:24.900
Hello?

00:16:33.950 --> 00:16:34.950
You know...

00:16:35.330 --> 00:16:40.000
I told you to find elements
we can publish as an article in Mumu.

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:41.290
If you really want to do this,

00:16:41.290 --> 00:16:45.590
do it after you prove this girl Aria can cause
supernatural phenomena with black magic.

00:16:45.590 --> 00:16:46.420
That's all.

00:16:47.750 --> 00:16:49.510
So harsh!

00:16:51.720 --> 00:16:54.090
Now, what should I do?

00:16:58.520 --> 00:17:00.770
Many people

00:16:59.930 --> 00:17:00.770
<i>Sumikaze...</i>

00:17:01.140 --> 00:17:01.850
<i>Yes?</i>

00:17:02.230 --> 00:17:05.360
<i>Is there something you remember
from a dream you've had recently?</i>

00:17:05.360 --> 00:17:09.480
<i>If there are words to describe images
of that dream, I'd like you to list a few.</i>

00:17:10.360 --> 00:17:13.280
<i>I don't remember any concrete details.</i>

00:17:13.280 --> 00:17:14.860
<i>It's okay if they're fragmental.</i>

00:17:15.320 --> 00:17:16.410
<i>In that case...</i>

00:17:16.870 --> 00:17:22.250
<i>"Water's bottom," "moonlight,"
"many people"... I think.</i>

00:17:23.160 --> 00:17:24.370
<i>I see.</i>

00:17:24.370 --> 00:17:25.880
Many people

00:17:24.790 --> 00:17:25.880
<i>It's from back then...</i>

00:17:26.670 --> 00:17:29.000
<i>Why did Professor ask such a thing?</i>

00:17:29.670 --> 00:17:32.510
<i>I wonder if he was going to use it
as a topic in his series?</i>

00:17:35.010 --> 00:17:37.180
Though, I can't have him tell me anymore.

00:17:41.850 --> 00:17:43.230
Yes, Sumikaze here.

00:17:48.310 --> 00:17:49.150
Chi?

00:17:51.820 --> 00:17:54.070
Apparently their daughter
has gone missing.

00:17:54.070 --> 00:17:55.240
Oh, is that so?

00:17:55.240 --> 00:17:58.120
The police are coming in and out
since morning. It's a huge deal!

00:17:58.120 --> 00:18:00.830
I just hope it's not
a terrible case or anything!

00:18:03.710 --> 00:18:04.540
Hello?

00:18:09.590 --> 00:18:12.260
<i>I'm sure the cops already got my name.</i>

00:18:12.710 --> 00:18:14.670
You heard about
Professor Hashigami's case?

00:18:14.670 --> 00:18:17.510
Yeah, I heard. Apparently
they haven't caught who did it yet.

00:18:17.760 --> 00:18:21.220
It's so shocking.
I liked that professor, too.

00:18:21.220 --> 00:18:23.100
I hope the culprit gets caught soon.

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:25.060
Apparently there's some
eyewitness information, too,

00:18:25.060 --> 00:18:26.850
so I'm sure the cops will nab him soon.

00:18:26.850 --> 00:18:28.360
You think so?

00:18:28.360 --> 00:18:30.820
Keyhole... I have to find the keyhole.

00:18:31.610 --> 00:18:32.860
Keyhole...

00:18:35.820 --> 00:18:36.860
Keyhole!

00:18:41.490 --> 00:18:42.290
Go in...

00:18:42.870 --> 00:18:44.160
Please go in.

00:18:44.750 --> 00:18:47.210
Why aren't you going in?

00:18:53.710 --> 00:18:54.840
Keyhole...

00:18:55.170 --> 00:18:57.550
I have to find it... for my own good.

00:19:03.140 --> 00:19:05.520
MEMORIAL SERVICES FOR
THE LATE ISAYUKI HASHIGAMI

00:19:07.390 --> 00:19:08.400
THE LATE ISAYUKI HASHIGAMI

00:19:23.660 --> 00:19:26.000
At this rate... I'm a criminal!

00:19:26.370 --> 00:19:28.580
This wasn't how it was supposed to be!

00:19:29.040 --> 00:19:31.500
Why did I go to a place like that?

00:19:34.300 --> 00:19:35.340
Keyhole...

00:19:39.800 --> 00:19:41.010
Go in.

00:19:41.590 --> 00:19:42.640
Go in!

00:19:45.520 --> 00:19:47.890
Why is it... Why am I in such a...

00:19:58.240 --> 00:19:59.740
S-Stop it!

00:20:01.570 --> 00:20:03.160
Don't look at me!

00:20:09.210 --> 00:20:11.170
<i>Shut out all external information.</i>

00:20:11.670 --> 00:20:13.040
<i>Ignore everyone's glances.</i>

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:15.800
<i>I am not being watched by anyone.</i>

00:20:15.800 --> 00:20:17.670
<i>I'm fine! I'm fine! I'm fine!</i>

00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:28.730
Hello?

00:20:36.360 --> 00:20:37.820
D-Devil?

00:20:42.950 --> 00:20:44.120
Why?

00:20:53.540 --> 00:20:54.210
March 1st (Tuesday)

00:20:57.340 --> 00:20:59.210
It was all a dream?

00:21:01.090 --> 00:21:01.880
It can't be...

00:21:01.880 --> 00:21:06.010
<i>Jeez, you're that old, and you still
wet the bed! So embarrassing!</i>

00:21:08.810 --> 00:21:10.680
Th-Th-This isn't a dream, right?

00:21:10.680 --> 00:21:11.980
<i>The fact that you wet your bed?</i>

00:21:11.980 --> 00:21:14.900
I-I-I mean you! You! You're talking, right?

00:21:14.900 --> 00:21:16.900
<i>I'm completely inconsequential.</i>

00:21:17.150 --> 00:21:19.690
<i>Besides, there's a huge crisis!
Turn on your TV!</i>

00:21:19.690 --> 00:21:22.360
It's not inconsequential!
What in the world are you?

00:21:22.360 --> 00:21:23.740
Because of you, I—

00:21:23.030 --> 00:21:25.870
<i>Shut up! Just turn on the TV! Hurry!</i>

00:21:37.290 --> 00:21:48.930
MITAKA CITY MASS SUICIDE
51 BODIES FOUND SO FAR
IN INOKASHIRA PARK

00:21:37.630 --> 00:21:40.510
<i>The newest police report has just come in.</i>

00:21:40.840 --> 00:21:44.760
<i>The total number of corpses
found so far is n-now 51?</i>

00:21:45.010 --> 00:21:46.550
<i>There are 51 corpses now!</i>

00:21:46.550 --> 00:21:48.930
<i>They are saying
the number may grow even further!</i>

00:21:53.520 --> 00:21:53.850
POLICE

00:21:58.270 --> 00:21:59.690
<i>Recapping the situation now!</i>

00:21:59.940 --> 00:22:03.740
<i>Early this morning, in the pond
within Inokashira Park in Mitaka City, Tokyo,</i>

00:22:03.740 --> 00:22:06.820
<i>at least 50 corpses have been found.</i>

00:22:06.820 --> 00:22:07.660
<i>Furthermore,</i>

00:22:07.910 --> 00:22:11.370
<i>over 100 more corpses are speculated
to be sunken within the lake!</i>

00:22:11.750 --> 00:22:13.540
What's that about?

